        "original_id": "35e2732e-1550-5645-a03b-8571e86e2de4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Weinreich, Uriel Weinreich\n- Places: Kuldīga, Russian Empire, Latvia, New York City, United States\n- Roles: linguist, father\n- Topics: sociolinguistics, Yiddish\n- Products: Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary\n\nFacts:\n- Max Weinreich was born on 22 April 1894 in Kuldīga in the Russian Empire, now Latvia.\n- Uriel Weinreich was born on 23 May 1926 and was a Polish-American linguist.\n- Uriel Weinreich edited the Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary.\n- Max Weinreich was a Russian Jewish linguist who specialized in sociolinguistics and Yiddish.\n- Max Weinreich was the father of the linguist Uriel Weinreich.\n- Uriel Weinreich died on 30 March 1967.\n- Max Weinreich died on 29 January 1969 in New York City, United States.",
